## 5. DEVELOPMENT WORKFLOW

For every feature (see full doc §72–76):

1. **Understand** — inspect repo + graphify; read scope/design refs
2. **Plan** — reuse components, identify API/state/a11y/brand needs
3. **Implement** — existing architecture + Quirri design system
4. **Integrate** — connect to app; no isolated demo code in `src/`
5. **Validate** — function, responsive, a11y, brand, loading/empty/error states
6. **Refine** — remove duplicates, arbitrary values, clutter
7. **Report** — what changed, files touched, decisions, assumptions, open issues

### 5.1 Playwright (mandatory for UI)

For **any** design change or visual/layout bug report:

1. Use the **Playwright** MCP (`user-playwright`) — navigate, log in as Super Admin, screenshot, and hit-test.
2. Prefer seeded Super Admin credentials from the API seed script — never echo passwords in chat.
3. Confirm open + collapsed / before + after when the bug is state-dependent (e.g. sidebar toggle).
4. Do not mark UI work done until Playwright evidence shows the fix.

### 5.2 Tooltips (mandatory)

- **Forbidden:** native HTML `title` attributes for hover hints (OS black/yellow tooltips).
- **Required:** Quirri floating tips via `useQuirriTip` / `QuirriTooltip` (`src/components/superadmin/QuirriTooltip.jsx`).
- **Look:** white card, Ink text, `--line` border, `--shadow-md`, Poppins 12px / medium, `--radius` (8px), calm — never solid black panels.
- Icon-only controls still need `aria-label`; the tip is supplementary.
- Use for collapsed sidebar labels, icon buttons, and any truncated name that needs a hover reveal.

### 5.3 Product UI — dropdowns & text (mandatory)

Full contract: `docs/QUIRRI_PRODUCT_UI_RULES.md` · rule file: `.cursor/rules/quirri-product-ui.mdc`

- **Dropdowns:** `QuirriSelect` (or labeled `quirri-select`); first option `All…` / `Select…`; 44px min-height; `aria-label` if no visible label.
- **Text:** left-align titles/labels/body; right-align `.num`; center only login brand card; label → control → hint|error.
- **Fonts:** Poppins for portals and auth (Brand v1.0).
- **Must-haves:** no mocks, one amber CTA, catalog fields, empty/error when API missing, Playwright for UI checks.
- Applies to **existing and all future** builds — do not invent per-page layout or select styles.

